function validateString(input) {
  let digitsCount = 0;
  let specialCharsCount = 0;
  let capitalLettersCount = 0;

  for (let i = 0; i < input.length; i++) {
    const char = input[i];

    if (/[0-9]/.test(char)) {
      digitsCount++;
    } else if (/[^A-Za-z0-9]/.test(char)) {
      specialCharsCount++;
    } else if (/[A-Z]/.test(char)) {
      capitalLettersCount++;
    }

    // Check if all criteria are met
    if (digitsCount >= 2 && specialCharsCount >= 2 && capitalLettersCount >= 2) {
      return true;
    }
  }

  return false;
}
```

This function uses a loop to iterate over each character in the input string and counts the number of digits, special characters, and capital letters encountered. It uses regular expressions to match the different types of characters.

The function returns `true` if all the criteria are met (i.e., at least 2 digits, 2 special characters, and 2 capital letters), and `false` otherwise.

The time complexity of this function is O(n) because it loops through each character in the input string once. The space complexity is O(1) because it only uses a constant amount of additional memory to store the counts.

