Here is the JavaScript function that sorts an array of strings in alphabetical order based on the length of the strings:

```javascript
function sortArray(arr) {
  var n = arr.length;

  // Bubble sort algorithm
  for (var i = 0; i < n-1; i++) {
    for (var j = 0; j < n-i-1; j++) {
      // Compare the lengths of two adjacent strings
      if (arr[j].length > arr[j+1].length) {
        var temp = arr[j];
        arr[j] = arr[j+1];
        arr[j+1] = temp;
      }
      // If two strings have the same length, compare lexicographically
      else if (arr[j].length === arr[j+1].length && arr[j] > arr[j+1]) {
        var temp = arr[j];
        arr[j] = arr[j+1];
        arr[j+1] = temp;
      }
    }
  }

  return arr;
}
```

This function uses the bubble sort algorithm to compare the lengths of adjacent strings in the array. If the length of the current string is greater than the length of the next string, the two strings are swapped. If the lengths are equal, the strings are compared lexicographically and swapped if necessary.

