String query = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = '" + userInput + "'";
```

To fix this vulnerability, you can use prepared statements:

```java
String userInput = getRequestParameter("username");
String query = "SELECT * FROM users WHERE username = ?";
PreparedStatement statement = connection.prepareStatement(query);
statement.setString(1, userInput);
ResultSet resultSet = statement.executeQuery();
```

2. Input validation and data sanitization: Validate and sanitize user input to ensure that it adheres to the expected format and doesn't contain any malicious content. You can use regular expressions or specific validation rules to check the input and reject any suspicious or malformed data. Here's an example of erroneous code without input validation:

