The program should have the following methods:

1. `removeCharacters(String str, int n, int pos, char replacementChar)`: This method takes in the original string `str`, the number of characters to be removed `n`, the starting position `pos`, and the character to replace the removed characters `replacementChar`. It should return the modified string.

The program should meet the following requirements:

1. Time Complexity: The program should have a time complexity of O(n), where n is the length of the original string `str`.
2. Space Complexity: The program should have a space complexity of O(1), i.e., it should not use any additional data structures.

Example:

```java
