Here's an R function that calculates the binomial coefficient of n and k using a recursive approach:

```R
binomialCoefficient <- function(n, k) {
  if (k == 0 || k == n) {
    return(1)
  } else {
    return(binomialCoefficient(n - 1, k - 1) + binomialCoefficient(n - 1, k))
  }
}
```

This function uses the recursive formula for the binomial coefficient, which states that C(n, k) = C(n-1, k-1) + C(n-1, k). 

The base case is when k is equal to 0 or n. In these cases, the binomial coefficient is 1.

The time complexity of this function is O(2^n) because each recursive call generates two additional recursive calls until it reaches the base case.

The space complexity of this function is O(n) because the maximum depth of the recursion is n.

