Here's the JavaScript code for the function to calculate the nth term in the Lucas series:

```javascript
function lucasSeries(n) {
  if (n === 1) {
    return 2;
  } else if (n === 2) {
    return 1;
  } else {
    let term1 = 2;
    let term2 = 1;
    let currentTerm;

    for (let i = 3; i <= n; i++) {
      currentTerm = term1 + term2;
      term1 = term2;
      term2 = currentTerm;
    }

    return currentTerm;
  }
}
```

To use this function and calculate the nth term in the Lucas series, you can call the function with the desired value of n. For example:

