console.log(lucasSeries(6)); // Output: 11
```

The function checks if n is 1 or 2, in which case it returns the corresponding values directly. For n greater than 2, it uses a loop to calculate the nth term by iteratively summing the previous two terms. The loop starts from i = 3, as the first two terms are already known. Finally, the function returns the calculated nth term.

