Here's a Java program that reads two positive prime numbers from the user and prints the sum of their prime factors. It also validates that the input numbers are prime numbers and terminates if the input numbers are not prime:

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class PrimeFactorsSum {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);

        // Read the first number
        System.out.print("Enter the first positive prime number: ");
        int num1 = scanner.nextInt();

        // Check if the first number is prime
        if (!isPrime(num1)) {
            System.out.println("Input is not a prime number. Program terminated.");
            System.exit(0);
        }

        // Read the second number
        System.out.print("Enter the second positive prime number: ");
        int num2 = scanner.nextInt();

        // Check if the second number is prime
        if (!isPrime(num2)) {
            System.out.println("Input is not a prime number. Program terminated.");
            System.exit(0);
        }

        // Calculate and print the sum of prime factors
        int sum = sumOfPrimeFactors(num1) + sumOfPrimeFactors(num2);
        System.out.println("Sum of prime factors: " + sum);

        scanner.close();
    }

    // Function to check if a number is prime
    public static boolean isPrime(int number) {
        if (number <= 1) {
            return false;
        }

        for (int i = 2; i <= Math.sqrt(number); i++) {
            if (number % i == 0) {
                return false;
            }
        }

        return true;
    }

    // Function to calculate the sum of prime factors of a number
    public static int sumOfPrimeFactors(int number) {
        int sum = 0;

        for (int i = 2; i <= number; i++) {
            if (number % i == 0 && isPrime(i)) {
                sum += i;
            }
        }

        return sum;
    }
}
```

In this program, the `isPrime()` function is used to check if a number is prime or not. The `sumOfPrimeFactors()` function calculates the sum of prime factors for a given number. The main logic is in the `main()` function where the user inputs two positive prime numbers, validates their primality, and calculates the sum of their prime factors.

