You can find the sum of all the digits in a given number by converting the number to a string, and then iterating over each character in the string to get the numerical value of each digit and summing them up. Here's a Java program that does this:

```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class SumOfDigits {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);
        System.out.print("Enter a positive integer: ");
        int number = scanner.nextInt();

        int sum = findSumOfDigits(number);
        System.out.println("Sum of digits: " + sum);
    }

    public static int findSumOfDigits(int number) {
        int sum = 0;
        String numberString = String.valueOf(number);
        for (int i = 0; i < numberString.length(); i++) {
            char digitChar = numberString.charAt(i);
            int digitValue = digitChar - '0'; // convert char to int
            sum += digitValue;
        }
        return sum;
    }
}
```

