```java
public static int findKthLargest(int[] arr, int k) {
    // Convert k to its equivalent index
    int index = arr.length - k;

    // Call the helper method to find the kth largest element
    return findKthLargestHelper(arr, 0, arr.length - 1, index);
}

private static int findKthLargestHelper(int[] arr, int start, int end, int k) {
    // Choose a pivot element
    int pivotIndex = partition(arr, start, end);

    // If the pivot is at the kth index, return it
    if (pivotIndex == k) {
        return arr[pivotIndex];
    }

    // If the pivot is greater than k, search the left subarray
    if (pivotIndex > k) {
        return findKthLargestHelper(arr, start, pivotIndex - 1, k);
    }

    // If the pivot is less than k, search the right subarray
    return findKthLargestHelper(arr, pivotIndex + 1, end, k);
}

private static int partition(int[] arr, int start, int end) {
    // Choose the rightmost element as the pivot
    int pivot = arr[end];

    // Index of the smaller element
    int i = start - 1;

    for (int j = start; j < end; j++) {
        // If current element is smaller than or equal to the pivot
        if (arr[j] <= pivot) {
            i++;

            // Swap arr[i] and arr[j]
            int temp = arr[i];
            arr[i] = arr[j];
            arr[j] = temp;
        }
    }

    // Swap arr[i+1] and arr[end] (pivot)
    int temp = arr[i + 1];
    arr[i + 1] = arr[end];
    arr[end] = temp;

    // Return the index of the pivot element
    return i + 1;
}
```

To find the k-th largest element in the array, we use the Quickselect algorithm. The partition() method is used to choose a pivot element and rearrange the array such that all elements smaller than the pivot are on the left and all elements greater than the pivot are on the right. We then recursively search the appropriate subarray based on the pivot index.

The time complexity of this method is O(n) since we are partitioning the array in each recursion and reducing the search space by half.

