```java
import java.util.Scanner;

public class AddLargeNumbers {

    public static String add(String num1, String num2) {
        StringBuilder result = new StringBuilder();

        int carry = 0;
        int i = num1.length() - 1;
        int j = num2.length() - 1;

        while (i >= 0 || j >= 0 || carry != 0) {
            int digit1 = i >= 0 ? num1.charAt(i--) - '0' : 0;
            int digit2 = j >= 0 ? num2.charAt(j--) - '0' : 0;

            int sum = digit1 + digit2 + carry;
            carry = sum / 10;
            int digit = sum % 10;

            result.insert(0, digit);
        }

        return result.toString();
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner scanner = new Scanner(System.in);

        System.out.print("Enter the first number: ");
        String num1 = scanner.nextLine();

        System.out.print("Enter the second number: ");
        String num2 = scanner.nextLine();

        String sum = add(num1, num2);
        System.out.println("Sum: " + sum);
    }
}
```

This program uses a StringBuilder to store the result of the addition. It iterates through the digits of both numbers from right to left, adding the corresponding digits and the carry value. The carry value is updated by dividing the sum by 10, and the digit value is the remainder of the sum divided by 10. The digit is then inserted at the beginning of the result StringBuilder. Finally, the result is converted to a String and printed as the sum of the two numbers.

