The `merge` function takes two sorted arrays (`leftHalf` and `rightHalf`) and merges them into a single sorted array (`result`). It compares elements from both arrays, adds the smaller element to the result array, and advances the corresponding index. After one of the arrays is fully processed, it adds the remaining elements from the other array to the result.

