Here is an implementation of the exponential moving average function in R:

```R
ema <- function(x, alpha = 0.5) {
  if (length(x) == 0) {
    return(vector())
  }
  if (alpha < 0 || alpha > 1) {
    stop("Smoothing factor (alpha) must be between 0 and 1.")
  }

  ema_values <- vector(length = length(x))
  ema_values[1] <- x[1]

  for (i in 2:length(x)) {
    ema_values[i] <- alpha * x[i] + (1 - alpha) * ema_values[i - 1]
  }

  return(ema_values)
}
```

To use the function, you can simply pass a vector of numbers as the input, and optionally specify the smoothing factor (alpha) as a second parameter. If not specified, the function will use a default smoothing factor of 0.5.

