2. We iterate through each element of the array and add it to the min heap.
3. If the size of the min heap exceeds k, we remove the smallest element from the min heap.
4. Finally, we return the smallest element remaining in the min heap, which will be the kth largest element in the array.
5. In the `main` method, we provide an example array `nums` and the value of k (4 in this case) to find the 4th largest element in the array.
