```csharp
public static int StringToInteger(string str)
{
    // Ignore leading and trailing white spaces
    str = str.Trim();

    // Check if the string is empty
    if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(str))
    {
        return 0;
    }

    int sign = 1;
    int index = 0;
    int result = 0;

    // Check if the number is negative
    if (str[index] == '-' || str[index] == '+')
    {
        sign = (str[index] == '-') ? -1 : 1;
        index++;
    }

    // Iterate through the remaining characters
    while (index < str.Length)
    {
        // Check if the character is a digit
        if (char.IsDigit(str[index]))
        {
            int digit = str[index] - '0';

            // Check if the result will exceed the integer range
            if (result > int.MaxValue / 10 || (result == int.MaxValue / 10 && digit > int.MaxValue % 10))
            {
                return (sign == 1) ? int.MaxValue : int.MinValue;
            }

            // Update the result
            result = result * 10 + digit;
        }
        else
        {
            // Return 0 if any non-digit character is found
            return 0;
        }

        index++;
    }

    return result * sign;
}
```

This implementation uses a simple algorithm to convert the string to an integer value. It starts by trimming the string to remove leading and trailing white spaces. Then, it checks if the string is empty and returns 0 if it is. 

Next, it initializes a variable to store the sign of the number (1 for positive, -1 for negative) and an index variable to iterate through the characters of the string. If the first character is a plus (+) or minus (-) sign, it updates the sign accordingly and moves the index to the next character.

Then, it iterates through the remaining characters of the string. For each character, it checks if it is a digit. If it is, it converts the digit character to its numeric value and updates the result by multiplying it by 10 and adding the digit value. It also checks if the result will exceed the integer range during this process and returns the maximum or minimum value accordingly.

If any non-digit character is found during the iteration, it returns 0.

Finally, it multiplies the result by the sign variable and returns the final value.

