The `factorial_recursion` function also takes an integer `n` as input. It uses recursion to calculate the factorial by multiplying `n` with the factorial of `n-1`. The base case is when `n` is 0, in which case it returns 1. Similar to `factorial_while_loop`, it returns an error message for invalid input or negative numbers.

